WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:17.496
Magrib paced back and forth in the hot sun.

2
00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:20.697
He did not hear Aladdin's call for help.

3
00:00:22.057 --> 00:00:25.178
He was thinking about the lamp and making big plans.

4
00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:29.599
"Soon I will be richer than any king!"

5
00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:31.920
he said with an evil grin.

6
00:00:34.048 --> 00:00:37.229
"I will be the most powerful man on earth!"

7
00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:41.170
Magrib laughed and did a merry little dance.

8
00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:47.812
Then he stopped and frowned.

9
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:50.253
"Where is that boy?

10
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:52.373
He has been gone too long."

11
00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.694
Suddenly Magrib touched his ear.

12
00:00:56.374 --> 00:00:57.435
Had he heard something?

13
00:00:57.455 --> 00:01:00.616
"Uncle! I am back!

14
00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:01.976
Can you hear me?"

15
00:01:02.548 --> 00:01:04.149
It was Aladdin calling again.

16
00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:08.790
Magrib ran to the opening in the earth and looked over the edge.

17
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.391
"What are you doing, boy?

18
00:01:11.911 --> 00:01:12.891
Come up right now!"

19
00:01:12.911 --> 00:01:16.892
"Uncle, I cannot," answered Aladdin.

20
00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:20.173
"I am too heavy to climb this last step.

21
00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:23.334
My pockets are full and my jacket is bulging.

22
00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:27.336
I am carrying many pieces of glass fruit from the garden.

23
00:01:27.816 --> 00:01:28.636
Please help me up!"

24
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.783
"Just give me the lamp, boy," snapped Magrib.

25
00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:36.705
"It is the lamp that weighs you down.

26
00:01:37.986 --> 00:01:40.528
Give me the lamp and your load will be lighter."

27
00:01:40.548 --> 00:01:42.430
"The lamp?

28
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:43.731
Oh yes, the lamp.

29
00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:45.232
I have it here someplace.

30
00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:48.975
But, Uncle, it is not the lamp that weighs me down.

31
00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.436
The lamp is not heavy."

32
00:01:50.456 --> 00:01:53.138
"Where is the lamp?"

33
00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:55.020
asked Magrib eagerly.

34
00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.581
"What have you done with it?"

35
00:01:56.601 --> 00:02:01.168
"It's wrapped in my sash in my back pocket," said Aladdin.

36
00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:04.210
"I will gladly give it to you when I get up there.

37
00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.730
Please give me a hand!"

38
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.972
"Just give me the lamp, boy!"

39
00:02:09.352 --> 00:02:11.073
the magician shouted angrily.

40
00:02:11.093 --> 00:02:14.914
"I cannot reach the lamp," said Aladdin.

41
00:02:15.274 --> 00:02:18.756
"See?" He stretched his arm toward his back.

42
00:02:18.776 --> 00:02:21.397
"I am loaded with glass fruit.

43
00:02:21.697 --> 00:02:22.678
They are for my mother."

44
00:02:23.558 --> 00:02:24.838
He reached into a pocket.

45
00:02:24.858 --> 00:02:27.019
"Here is a sparkling red one.

46
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.260
You may have it!"

47
00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:32.069
"No!" screamed Magrib.

48
00:02:32.089 --> 00:02:34.691
"I don't want any jewels!

49
00:02:35.211 --> 00:02:36.452
I want only the lamp!

50
00:02:36.892 --> 00:02:37.792
Give it to me now!

51
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:42.655
NOW!" "I will, Uncle, I promise," said Aladdin firmly.

52
00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:44.276
"But I cannot give it to you yet."

53
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:49.479
Magrib leaned down so that Aladdin could see his angry face.

54
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.201
His cheeks were a terrible shade of red.

55
00:02:53.221 --> 00:02:56.783
"You refuse to obey me?"

56
00:02:57.263 --> 00:02:58.264
hissed the magician.

57
00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.881
"I cannot obey you," said Aladdin.

58
00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:08.484
"I―" Magrib threw back his head and screamed, "You cannot obey?"

59
00:03:09.504 --> 00:03:13.046
The magician stomped his feet until dust flew up around him.

60
00:03:14.206 --> 00:03:16.107
He pounded his head with his fists.

61
00:03:16.127 --> 00:03:18.688
"Cannot obey me?"

62
00:03:19.148 --> 00:03:19.889
he screamed.

63
00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:24.110
He pulled the silver box from his sleeve.

64
00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.552
"Will not obey ME?"

65
00:03:28.872 --> 00:03:33.034
Magrib grabbed a handful of the powder and muttered some magic words.

66
00:03:34.354 --> 00:03:36.975
"You will be sorry, you worthless boy!"

67
00:03:36.995 --> 00:03:39.677
"What are you doing, Uncle?"

68
00:03:40.017 --> 00:03:40.757
cried Aladdin.

69
00:03:40.777 --> 00:03:41.657
"Help me!"

70
00:03:42.858 --> 00:03:46.399
Magrib threw the powder onto the glowing ashes of the fire.

71
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.261
Flames shot into the air, higher than his head.

72
00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:54.463
"No, my boy, now you will never get out!"

73
00:03:54.843 --> 00:03:55.603
he screamed.

74
00:03:55.623 --> 00:04:00.897
"Uncle!" Once again, the ground shook.

75
00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:06.720
From the stone steps, Aladdin saw the marble door start to close over his head.

76
00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:11.062
The door to the enchanted treasury fell back into place.

77
00:04:12.123 --> 00:04:15.805
Then rocks and dirt rolled down and covered it completely.

78
00:04:17.486 --> 00:04:21.548
Magrib shook his fists at the sky and twisted his body in fury.

79
00:04:21.568 --> 00:04:25.150
"Aaaaargh!" he groaned.

80
00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.071
"Everything is ruined!"

81
00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:31.137
"Uncle!" Aladdin shouted into the darkness.

82
00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:35.427
"UNCLE!" No one heard him.

83
00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:36.630
No one answered.
